# Backend conventions

## Package ownership

| Package | Owns |
|---------|------|
| `api` | HTTP only — map requests/responses |
| `services` | Pipeline orchestration |
| `ocr` | OCR port + adapters |
| `preprocessing` | Image validate/preprocess |
| `extraction` | Field extraction from OCR evidence |
| `normalization` | Canonical value forms |
| `rules` | Deterministic checks (source-documented) |
| `confidence` | PASS/REVIEW/FAIL policy from evidence |
| `ai` | Provider interface; OpenAI adapter only here |
| `persistence` | SQLite / repositories |
| `batch` | Concurrency-limited batch jobs |
| `core` | Config, exceptions, timing |
| `models` | Shared Pydantic models |

## Result status

Use only `PASS`, `REVIEW`, `FAIL`. Include explanation and decision method on every check result. Include `processing_time_ms` on verification results.

## Errors

Do not swallow exceptions. Convert to explicit failure/REVIEW with explanation, or re-raise after logging.

## Rules modules

When implementing a rule, module docs must identify: requirement, authoritative source, PASS/REVIEW/FAIL criteria, limitations (see `docs/RULES.md`).
